"new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGATA, SHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKECHI, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, SHUN'ICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A coating liquid for a photocatalyst-containing coating film which comprises an organic coloring matter and can be used for confirming the formation of a film and checking the photocatalytic activity of the film after the coating liquid is applied on a substrate; and a method for applying the coating liquid. By utilizing a coating liquid comprising an organic coloring matter, the formation of a film can be confirmed after a transparent photocatalyst-containing coating liquid is applied. By utilizing a coating liquid comprising an organic coloring matter containing a metal element in its molecule, a film formed from the coating liquid can be checked for the photocatalytic activity thereof.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un liquide d'enduit destiné à un film d'enduit contenant un photocatalyseur, le liquide d'enduit comprenant un colorant organique et pouvant s'utiliser pour vérifier la formation d'un film et contrôler l'activité photocatalytique du film après l'application du liquide d'enduit sur un substrat. L'invention concerne également un procédé d'application du liquide d'enduit. L'utilisation d'un liquide d'enduit comprenant un colorant organique permet de vérifier la formation d'un film après l'application d'un liquide d'enduit contenant un photocatalyseur transparent. L'utilisation d'un liquide d'enduit comprenant un colorant organique contenant un élément métallique dans sa molécule permet de contrôler l'activité photocatalytique d'un film formé à partir du liquide d'enduit.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>